// Function-body non-deterministic MODIFIERS (`fn f() forall { … }`) inside spec
// functions. A modifier records its kind on the function's body block, lowered
// by a different codegen path (`visit_function_definition_body`) than an inline
// block. In proof mode every spec-function body is lowered, and the two kinds
// here lower identically: vanilla WASM, no wrapper opcode, each `@` hoisted
// into a hidden trailing choice parameter. Where they stay apart is the
// obligation — the `forall` one is universal and its body is omitted from the
// emitted module record, the `exists` one travels as an exists-kind
// `inference.hspecs` entry and its body is retained as that judgment's subject
// — and that split is read from the typed AST, never from the bytes. Having the
// pair in one module is what makes the identical lowering and the differing
// obligations observable together. This is the spec-wrapped, analysis-legal
// counterpart of the negative fixture `nondet_body_modifiers.inf`; the `assume`
// body modifier, which stays a P001 rejection, lives in
// `spec_assume_body_modifier.inf`.
spec NondetBodyModifiers {
  fn forall_fn() forall {
    let x: i32 = @;
    assert(x == x);
  }
  fn exists_fn() exists {
    let y: i32 = @;
    assert(y == y);
  }
}
